♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:30.002
- When I was in the seventh grade,

00:06:30.002 --> 00:06:32.083
my buddy moved away to Oregon.

00:06:32.083 --> 00:06:34.112
There was a week where I went up

00:06:34.112 --> 00:06:35.750
to go visit him in Portland.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.071
I flew up there by
myself, go to his house,

00:06:38.071 --> 00:06:39.078
and the whole thing was is,

00:06:39.078 --> 00:06:40.707
"Hey, he's going to be in school

00:06:40.707 --> 00:06:41.960
"on some of these days this week.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.001
"So you can shadow him to school

00:06:44.001 --> 00:06:46.648
"or you can hang out until
he gets out of school."

00:06:46.648 --> 00:06:47.739
I shadowed him one day and I was like,

00:06:47.739 --> 00:06:49.841
"This is weird, I'm going to
stay at your house and wait."

00:06:49.841 --> 00:06:52.058
But in his room, there were four things

00:06:52.058 --> 00:06:54.146
that were very important,

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:56.151
A Stiff Little Fingers record,

00:06:56.151 --> 00:07:00.586
there was a All record,
a Dinosaur Junior record,

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.311
and there was an electric guitar.

00:07:03.311 --> 00:07:06.729
So what I did was, I would play
those three albums on vinyl

00:07:06.729 --> 00:07:09.009
and I would go over
and pick up this guitar

00:07:09.009 --> 00:07:10.898
to keep myself entertained
throughout the day

00:07:10.898 --> 00:07:13.368
for those three or four days
that he would be at school

00:07:13.368 --> 00:07:14.230
until he would come back.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:16.570
And we'd skate at night and do whatever.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.384
That changed my life you know.

00:07:18.384 --> 00:07:20.169
Changed my life.

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:24.336
The hearing punk rock music
and picking up the guitar,

00:07:25.471 --> 00:07:29.378
something clicked where it's almost like

00:07:29.378 --> 00:07:30.850
there's a bunch of gasoline on the ground

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.888
and someone flicks a
cigarette, it just ignites.

00:07:32.888 --> 00:07:35.479
You know, it's just, it
was a chemical reaction

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:38.068
that just flipped on a switch

00:07:38.068 --> 00:07:41.410
that nothing could take
that guitar out of my hand

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.640
from that point forward.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.138
- Well my message to the
youth, pretty much, man,

00:07:44.138 --> 00:07:45.749
is just to follow your dreams.

00:07:45.749 --> 00:07:46.582
You know what I mean?

00:07:46.582 --> 00:07:48.048
I think a lot of people get caught up

00:07:48.048 --> 00:07:52.279
and get sidetracked by
what's happening around them

00:07:52.279 --> 00:07:53.339
and what's cool.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:55.089
People always ignore they gift,

00:07:55.089 --> 00:07:56.479
not realizing that gift is what's going to

00:07:56.479 --> 00:07:57.588
take you out of your poverty,

00:07:57.588 --> 00:07:59.068
take you out of your situation.

00:07:59.068 --> 00:08:03.057
That gift is the ultimate
element that God provided

00:08:03.057 --> 00:08:05.039
for you to get you out of any situation,

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:07.120
or to take you to what's destined for you.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.578
You know, some people are
just great at certain things

00:08:09.578 --> 00:08:14.518
but because music, or
modeling, or a film is cool,

00:08:14.518 --> 00:08:16.028
they alienate what their gifts are

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:19.519
just be a part of something
that is presumed to be

00:08:19.519 --> 00:08:21.139
or persuaded to be cool.

00:08:21.139 --> 00:08:23.069
So I always felt like, you know, my method

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:25.969
and message always has been
to just follow the gift

00:08:25.969 --> 00:08:28.327
that you have, put a
lot of emphasizing it,

00:08:28.327 --> 00:08:30.468
concentrate on what you
feel that you're great in,

00:08:30.468 --> 00:08:32.688
because what you're great in
is always what pulls you out

00:08:32.688 --> 00:08:35.479
of the worst situations
that you could ever imagine

00:08:35.479 --> 00:08:37.718
and put you in a better situation
life than you're in today.

00:08:37.718 --> 00:08:39.459
- Your gift can be anything.

00:08:39.459 --> 00:08:41.189
You can't look at it as simply running,

00:08:41.189 --> 00:08:43.009
jumping, singing, and dancing.

00:08:43.009 --> 00:08:44.098
But I tell you one thing,

00:08:44.098 --> 00:08:47.517
your gift is the thing that
you do the absolute best

00:08:47.517 --> 00:08:49.450
with the least amount of effort.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:51.499
For me, it was comedy.

00:08:51.499 --> 00:08:55.908
So once you identify, then
that's the beginning of it.

00:08:55.908 --> 00:08:57.889
But there's a lot of work to do,

00:08:57.889 --> 00:09:00.097
even after you identify your gift.

00:09:00.097 --> 00:09:02.935
You know, you can believe
you're something all you want,

00:09:02.935 --> 00:09:05.692
but if you don't work towards
it, you're just sitting there.

00:09:05.692 --> 00:09:06.733
It's going to be empty.

